# x a, element by element, for arrays x of two limbs and a scalar a that the program supplies (rule
# R3, the factors of a fused operation: architecture.md): the map scale_2 with the step
# scale_entry_step_2, which guards the limbs of each element and a first. scale_2's step only
# multiplies them; but a compiler that sees the elements of x to be 1 fuses a product a = y z of the
# program into the fms of mul_2_1 (Apple clang 21 under -ffp-contract=fast at -O2 with NDEBUG,
# measured: every round). Three additions more per element. Its claims are those of scale_2.
fold:          scale_2_entry
arrays:        supplied x = x0 x1
scalars:       supplied a
state:         mask finite
step:          z = scale_entry_step_2(x, a)
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z = z0 z1
check:         fold_finish_2
finish:        none
value:         x*a
requires:      canonical x
ensures:       entries z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldMaps.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldMaps.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        mul_2_1 on each element, its limbs and the scalar guarded (scale_entry_step_2)
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
